  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "While the default colliders in the hands are very nice, they can get in the way of physbones if you're trying to do anything clever with them and it would be nice if there was a toggle option like with Contacts to denote if they can be interacted with by just yourself or other players.  \neg; Allow Grabbing: \"All/Self/Others\"\nAllow Collision: \"All/Self/Others\"\nAllow Posing: \"All/Self/Others\"\nPersonal Usecase Examples; I have some floppy PhysBone-driven Turtles on an avatar that can be follow my hands or be set down in the world on a parent constraint.  They live in a world constraint \"beside\" my avatar's armature, so while they look cute and people can mess with them, they also slam right into the spheres on my hands and angle away from them when parented to each hand.  My workaround was to position the hand colliders to account for that below where the turtles would be on my hand instead of inside them. \nI also use PhysBones on the limbs of my avatars to give them a bit of floppy movement and let people grab them and wave them about.  Which I can sometimes do to myself on the same limb (ie; left hand Grabs left Arm's physbone).  Being able to set Grabbing on those physbones on my avatars limbs to other players only would fix this.",
